<section class="card"><h2>Coverage and uncertainty</h2><p>Previous-year calendar patterns need 366 observed dates and four comparable disjoint tests. A missing prior-year target, including an unmatched leap day, blocks that candidate. Fixed-date seasonal effects may be present in recorded values. Movable holidays use only the event dates recorded below. Event-assisted forecasts need two observed occurrences of each matching event, four shared disjoint test windows containing known events, and at least 5% lower error than the best simple model. Dates first entered today cannot enter earlier backtests. SEOcc assumes no holiday uplift.</p><p>Ranges use only completed saved endpoint errors for the same property binding, model version, selected method and horizon. The finite-sample 80% conformal quantile requires 20 disjoint forecasts. Time dependence and changing traffic mean this is an empirical target, not guaranteed probability coverage. Historical test errors are shown separately.</p><p><a href="<?= $view->e($base) ?>/performance">Review Search Console history →</a> · <a href="<?= $view->e($base) ?>/analytics">Review GA4 imports →</a></p></section>
